    "summary": "LatestMarketSnapshotStore compacts the append-only market snapshot journal when the file grows past 4x the byte length of one canonical line per live (symbol, dataset) key or past 32 MiB while containing superseded records. Compaction writes only the latest canonical line per (symbol, dataset) key (including any withdrawal tombstone that is the latest record for its key) in the identical line format to a sibling temporary file under exclusive flock on both the existing and replacement descriptors, fsyncs the temporary file, atomically replaces the journal via os.replace, and fsyncs the parent directory. Concurrent writers verify inode identity after acquiring flock and reopen if replaced."
